+## Group History Backfill
+
+Hermes can fetch recent Feishu group messages and prepend them to the current
+agent turn as `channel_context`. This lets the bot answer ordinary group
+follow-ups with recent room context without permanently importing the whole
+group transcript into Hermes conversation history.
+
+The Feishu API used is `GET /open-apis/im/v1/messages` with
+`container_id_type=chat`. Feishu requires the bot to be in the queried group.
+For app/tenant-token access to group history, the app must have a message-read
+scope plus `im:message.group_msg`.
+
+```yaml
+feishu:
+  history_backfill: true
+  history_backfill_limit: 20
+  history_backfill_seconds: 1800
+  history_backfill_max_chars: 6000
+  attachment_backfill_window_seconds: 300
+  attachment_backfill_max_messages: 3
+  attachment_backfill_max_files: 6
+  attachment_backfill_timeout_seconds: 8
+  assistant_user_ai_probability_threshold: 1.1  # >= 1.1 disables the global gate
+  assistant_user_ai_cooldown_seconds: 300        # 0 disables sender cooldown
+  assistant_identity_throttle_messages: 20
+  assistant_identity_throttle_seconds: 600
+```
+
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+|---------|---------|-------------|
+| `history_backfill` | `false` | Fetch recent group messages for the current turn |
+| `history_backfill_limit` | `20` | Maximum historical messages to include |
+| `history_backfill_seconds` | `1800` | Time window before the trigger message |
+| `history_backfill_max_chars` | `6000` | Maximum formatted context characters |
+| `attachment_backfill_window_seconds` | `300` | Same-sender window for a standalone image/file/video/audio followed by @Hermes |
+| `attachment_backfill_max_messages` | `3` | Maximum recent attachment messages recovered for one trigger |
+| `attachment_backfill_max_files` | `6` | Maximum files recovered for one trigger, including quoted attachments |
+| `attachment_backfill_timeout_seconds` | `8` | Attachment recovery deadline before a visible failure status is injected |
+| `assistant_user_ai_probability_threshold` | `1.1` (disabled) | Global threshold for any sender's `@assistant_user` message, including the configured human testing by mentioning themselves. Values below `1.1` enable isolated AI-authorship scoring; undisclosed AI-written messages at or above the threshold are refused locally before the main agent or tools run. A matching `people.yaml` entry may override this value for one sender. |
+| `assistant_user_ai_cooldown_seconds` | `300` | Per-sender cooldown after a confirmed refusal is delivered. During the cooldown, any later group trigger from that sender—`@assistant_user`, `@bot`, or both—receives a randomly selected short local response without classifier or main-agent inference. `0` disables cooldown. |
+| `assistant_identity_throttle_messages` | `20` | Suppress repeated assistant self-introductions if one appears in this many recent group messages |
+| `assistant_identity_throttle_seconds` | `600` | Suppress repeated assistant self-introductions if one appears in this many seconds |
+
+History backfill is skipped for Feishu DMs. Deleted messages, the trigger
+message, and Hermes' own prior bot messages are excluded from the context block.
+Merged forwarded messages (`merge_forward`) are expanded through the message
+detail API when possible; nested images and files are recovered as normal
+inbound attachments. Reply/history text contains only path-free placeholders;
+the resource bytes travel through the attachment pipeline exactly once.
+
+For a per-sender override, add the same key to that person's `people.yaml`
+entry. Matching uses Feishu `open_id`, `user_id`, or `union_id`, not the display
+name. For example:
+
+```yaml
+people:
+  - open_id: ou_example
+    name: Example User
+    assistant_user_ai_probability_threshold: 0.8
+```
+
+The classifier is an independent, tool-free auxiliary-model call. It receives
+only the current `@assistant_user` message and the single message directly
+quoted by it, if any. It does not receive channel history, the long-lived
+session, person-profile prose, attachment backfill, or previous Hermes answers.
+The sender ID is used locally only to resolve the configured threshold; neither
+that ID, the matched `people.yaml` record, nor the resolved threshold is sent to
+the classifier. The threshold is applied locally after scoring, so identical
+message-and-quote content produces an identical model request regardless of who
+sent it. Mention display names are replaced with `@person` before that request.
+This isolation applies only to the admission classifier. When a low score or an
+explicit AI disclosure passes the gate, Hermes resumes the unchanged normal
+reply path, including sender/group profile resolution and ordinary context.
+The quote is context for interpreting the current reply only; its author is not
+scored. Current text is capped at 4,000 characters and quoted text at 2,000
+characters. You may select a fast dedicated route with:
+
+```yaml
+auxiliary:
+  feishu_ai_authorship:
+    provider: auto
+    model: gpt-5.5
+    timeout: 30  # seconds; timeout/error falls back to the normal reply path
+    reasoning_effort: none
+```
+
+The admission call does not retry a transient failure on the same provider. Its
+request timeout is exposed as `auxiliary.feishu_ai_authorship.timeout`. The
+auxiliary response is parsed as `{probability, disclosed}`. Any finite
+numeric probability is normalized locally with `clip(0, 1)` and `round(...,
+1)`, so the value used for comparison is always one of `0.0`, `0.1`, ...,
+`1.0`. A high undisclosed score produces a fixed local refusal without exposing
+the score and without entering the main agent/tool loop, but only after that
+refusal is delivered successfully. A classifier error or timeout, or a failed
+refusal delivery, falls open to the unchanged normal reply path. Explicit
+disclosure of AI assistance also bypasses the refusal. A successfully delivered
+refusal starts the configured per-sender cooldown. Any further group trigger
+from that sender—including `@assistant_user`, `@bot`, or both—receives one
+randomly selected response from a local short-sentence pool, without another
+classifier or main-agent call until the interval expires. Unmentioned group
+messages and direct messages remain outside this cooldown. The pool uses a
+mildly angry first-person tone while criticizing only the behavior;
+each response places Chinese first and its English counterpart below, with the
+remaining cooldown seconds emphasized in bold. The interval is process-local,
+non-sliding, and resets on Gateway restart.
+
+## Missed Event Backfill
+
+`history_backfill` only adds context after Hermes has already received a trigger
+message. If the WebSocket connection was stale or offline when someone mentioned
+the bot, Hermes may not receive that trigger event until much later. Missed event
+backfill handles this transport recovery case separately: after startup, gateway
+reconnect, or the Lark SDK's internal WebSocket reconnect, Hermes scans recent
+messages in known chats and replays only unseen messages that pass the normal
+Feishu admission rules.
+
+The scan is bounded and does not enumerate the tenant. Target chats come from
+`missed_event_backfill_chats`, the Feishu home channel, explicit `group_rules`
+entries, and `~/.hermes/groups.yaml`. A wildcard `group_rules: "*"` authorizes
+normal inbound admission but is not used as a discovery source.
+
+Replayed messages admit exactly like live events. Each target chat's mode is
+resolved from chat metadata (`chat_mode`): DM targets — including a p2p home
+channel — replay without the group mention gate, while group targets still
+require a mention. If the metadata lookup fails, the chat is treated as a
+group so recovery can never widen admission. A message the user already
+re-asked via quote-reply (with or without a mention) is marked covered when
+that reply is answered, so the recovery scan does not answer it twice.
+
+```yaml
+feishu:
+  missed_event_backfill: true
+  missed_event_backfill_seconds: 21600
+  missed_event_backfill_limit: 50
+  missed_event_backfill_chats:
+    - oc_group_chat_id
+```
+
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+|---------|---------|-------------|
+| `missed_event_backfill` | `true` | Scan known Feishu chats after startup/reconnect for missed trigger messages |
+| `missed_event_backfill_seconds` | `21600` | Time window to scan before the recovery point |
+| `missed_event_backfill_limit` | `50` | Maximum listed messages per target chat |
+| `missed_event_backfill_chats` | `[]` | Extra chat IDs to scan in addition to home channel, explicit rules, and `groups.yaml` |
+
+The replay path uses the same message-id dedup cache as live events. When a user
+manually quotes an earlier missed message and mentions Hermes, the quoted
+message ID is marked covered after that turn is dispatched, so a later delayed
+push or reconnect scan does not answer the same original message again.
+
+For group replies, Hermes carries the current sender's Feishu `open_id` only as
+transport metadata. Every explicit `@name` or configured alias that resolves to
+an `open_id` in the hot-reloaded people index is replaced in place with Feishu's
+native inline Markdown mention syntax. If the answer does not explicitly
+mention the current sender, Hermes adds that native mention before the reply
+text. Both forms stay in the same `md.text` flow, so the client renders `@name`
+and the following prose on one line rather than as separate post blocks. Plain
+text fallback uses the same `<at user_id="...">...</at>` representation.
+Progress, retry, and internal status messages do not auto-mention the sender.
+
